put.description:
Update all roles for a user (replaces existing role assignments).
Useful for the frontend to sync role assignments.

Body:
    {
        "roles": ["DATA_ENGINEER", "BI_ANALYST"]
    }

Response:
    {
        "message": "Updated roles for user 'USERNAME'",
        "username": "USERNAME",
        "roles": ["DATA_ENGINEER", "BI_ANALYST"]
    }

get.description:
SSE endpoint for real-time cache invalidation events.

Establishes a persistent connection and pushes invalidation
events to the client in real-time (<50ms latency).

Supports reconnection via Last-Event-ID header — if the client
disconnects and reconnects, it can resume from where it left off.

Usage (JavaScript):
    const eventSource = new EventSource('/api/cache/stream');

    eventSource.addEventListener('cache_invalidation', (e) => {
        const data = JSON.parse(e.data);
        data.cache_keys.forEach(key => queryClient.invalidateQueries([key]));
    });

    eventSource.addEventListener('connected', (e) => {
        console.log('Connected:', JSON.parse(e.data));
    });

Response format (SSE):
    event: connected
    id: 1
    retry: 3000
    data: {"type":"connected","client_id":"abc-123",...}

    event: cache_invalidation
    id: 2
    data: {"type":"cache_invalidation","cache_keys":["users"],...}

post.description:
Check whether data has changed for a list of tables.

Compares current row timestamps against the last-known timestamps
stored in Redis. Returns a map of table_fqn -> has_changed (bool).
Frontend uses this to avoid unnecessary re-renders on tab switch.

Request body: {"tables": ["DB.SCHEMA.TABLE1", "DB.SCHEMA.TABLE2"]}
Response: {"DB.SCHEMA.TABLE1": true, "DB.SCHEMA.TABLE2": false}

